    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> be opposite vertices of a parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> if the diagonal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> then the area of the parallelogram is equal to",
